==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Heroic Musashi''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Awakened Musashi''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP after completing [[Eldritch Forces]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Musashi is an overall decent ranged anti-[[Wave Attack|Wave]] unit. He does a good job against most [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]], like [[Pigeon de Sable]], [[Kory]], and even [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|Hermit Cat]], provided you have a decent lineup to take the heat. Unlike [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]], his attack rate is too slow for him to fend for himself, meaning you must protect him well when using him in stages like [[Tiny Fists (Deadly)|Tiny Fists]].

The most important aspect of him is his Wave immunity, a respectable quality only replicated by certain [[Talents|Talented]] [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] or [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]], as well as [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] in [[Restriction Stage]]. However, as there's often a wide range of other options, you will be unlikely to use him unless you lack alternatives due to his sluggish recharge for his poor stats.

==='''True Form'''===
Awakened Musashi gains the Zombie Killer, Freeze Relic, and Immune to Curse abilities, along with increased health and attack power. Zombie Killer is an odd ability as he does not fare well against them, since common [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] will usually burrow into his range and knock him back, something exacerbated by his low KB count. He is, however, one of the only non-Uber [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] to outrange [[Cadaver Bear]].

His freeze ability against Relics isn't the worst, and serves as extra support, provided he isn't outranged by the Relic enemy in question ([[Loris]], [[Othom]], [[Lowkey]], [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]], etc.). The duration of his ability is a nice 3 seconds, which serves as reprieve for that amount of time. Immune to Curse serves to make it absolute that he will not lose his ability, but it isn't very useful, given his slow attack rate and low activation chance often preventing it from making an impact. Players who would want a consistent freeze effect would instead prefer to progress further and obtain [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]], since Doron, despite being a suicide bomber, is backed by his exceptional consistency.

His attack and health increases are very good, and allow him to remain semi-relevant to the [[Uncanny Legends]] meta. But, most importantly, this allows him to dominate in 4-Crown [[Stories of Legend]], which was a bit of an issue beforehand, meaning you will likely use him for Stories of Legend more than anything else. However, if you are looking for a good use of your Elder [[Catfruit]] and want to get a Cat that performs well in Uncanny Legends or for general use, then investing in [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], or [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] would be a better idea.

