==Trivia==
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] [[Version 5.10 Update|5.10]], Miyamoku Musashi was named Miyagi Musashi. This was likely a mistranslation, as 宮木 can be read as ''miyagi'' or ''miyamoku''.
*Prior to BCEN [[Version 8.0 Update|8.0]], Heroic Musashi was named Legendary Musashi.
*[[wikipedia:Miyamoto Musashi|Miyamoto Musashi]] was a famous Japanese samurai in ancient times who was also a writer as well as being well known for a swordsman. It was rumored that he won 61 duels in a row and was apparently a record. Unlike Miyamoku Musashi, he usually handled battles with two swords, which is shown in the [[True Form]] through a second, smaller sword.
*Awakened Musashi's Japanese description mentions that he stars in the drama "Unlucky Day Police"; the term meaning "Unlucky Day" is 仏滅 ''butsumetsu'', one of the six ''rokuyō'' (a cycle of days on the Japanese calendar, each with a different fortune). ''Butsumetsu'' symbolizes the day Buddha died and is considered to be the unluckiest of the ''rokuyō''.
*Since he's possessed by a ghost and his [[Inumusha|enemy form]] is a [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]], Miyamoku Musashi being the fourth [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] of Stories of Legend and having 400 range is likely a reference to how, in Japanese, one of the two pronunciations for the number 4 sounds exactly like the Japanese word for death.
*Since [[Version 13.0 Update|Version 13.0]], his [[Cat Guide]] entry incorrectly states that he can be obtained from [[Jail Break Tunnel]].
*Miyamoku Musashi is one of the units to have his descriptions rewritten in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], as "Unharmed by wave attacks" was changed to "Immune to Waves".

